window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-731168d993ec5d2b"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"subagents\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"_1\">子智能体</h1> <blockquote> <p>如需完整的文档索引，请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 后添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work 和 Codex 可以运行子智能体工作流：先并行启动各有专长的智能体，再将它们的结果汇总到一条回复中。这对于非常适合并行处理的复杂任务尤其有帮助，例如探索代码库或实施多步骤功能计划。</p> <p>在 Codex 本地客户端中，你还可以针对不同任务定义采用不同模型配置和指令的自定义智能体。</p> <p><a id=\"availability\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">可用性</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work 会向符合条件的账户显示子智能体工作流及其活动。</p> <p><a id=\"custom-agents\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>当前 Codex 版本默认启用子智能体工作流。你可以在 ChatGPT 桌面应用、Codex CLI 和 IDE 扩展中看到子智能体的活动。</p> <p>因为每个子智能体都会独立使用模型和工具，所以与效果相当的单智能体运行相比，子智能体工作流会消耗更多 token。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT Work 中，你可以要求 ChatGPT 将彼此独立的工作委派给子智能体。各智能体在 ChatGPT 的托管环境中运行，聊天界面会显示它们的活动和结果。在大多数智能等级下，需要明确要求进行委派。使用 Ultra 时，如果并行智能体能显著提升速度或质量，ChatGPT 可以主动委派工作。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在应用聊天中，要求 Codex 将互相独立的工作部分委派给子智能体。当前 Codex 本地版本会在你直接提出要求时，或适用的 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或技能指令提出要求时进行委派。应用会展示每个子智能体线程，方便你检查它的工作，以及它返回主聊天的摘要。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在交互式 CLI 会话中，要求 Codex 使用子智能体。Codex 也可以遵循适用的 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或技能指令来进行委派。子智能体运行期间，可使用 <code>/subagents</code> 检查各智能体线程并在它们之间切换。主线程会把子智能体的结果汇总到最终回复中。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 IDE 聊天中，要求 Codex 将互相独立的工作部分委派给子智能体。Codex 也可以遵循适用的 <code>AGENTS.md</code> 或技能指令来进行委派。当后台智能体界面可用时，正在运行的子智能体会显示在输入框上方。展开面板即可查看其状态、停止所有正在运行的子智能体，或打开某个子智能体线程。</p> <p><a id=\"why-subagent-workflows-help\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">子智能体工作流为何有用</h2> <p>即使上下文窗口很大，模型仍有其限制。如果主聊天（你在这里定义需求、约束和决策）被探索笔记、测试日志、堆栈跟踪和命令输出等嘈杂的中间内容淹没，会话的可靠性可能会随时间下降。</p> <p>这种情况通常被称为：</p> <ul> <li><strong>上下文污染（Context pollution）</strong>：有用信息被嘈杂的中间输出淹没。</li> <li><strong>上下文衰退（Context rot）</strong>：随着聊天中相关性较低的细节不断增加，性能逐渐下降。</li> </ul> <p>如需了解背景，请参阅 Chroma 关于<a href=\"https://research.trychroma.com/context-rot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">上下文衰退（需联网）</a>的文章。</p> <p>子智能体工作流会把嘈杂的工作移出主线程，从而缓解这些问题：</p> <ul> <li>让<strong>主智能体</strong>专注于需求、决策和最终输出。</li> <li>并行运行有专长的<strong>子智能体</strong>，分别负责探索、测试或日志分析。</li> <li>让子智能体返回<strong>摘要</strong>，而不是未经整理的中间输出。</li> </ul> <p>当工作可以独立并行推进时，子智能体还能节省时间；它们也可以把工作拆成边界明确的部分，使更大规模的任务更易处理。例如，Codex 可以把对数百万 token 文档的分析拆成更小的问题，再返回提炼后的要点。</p> <p>起步时，可以将并行智能体用于以读取为主的任务，例如探索、测试、分诊和总结。对于并行且写入量较大的工作流，应更加谨慎，因为多个智能体同时编辑代码可能造成冲突，并增加协调成本。</p> <p><a id=\"core-terms\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">核心术语</h2> <p>Codex 在子智能体工作流中会使用几个相互关联的术语：</p> <ul> <li><strong>子智能体工作流（Subagent workflow）</strong>：Codex 运行并行智能体并合并其结果的工作流。</li> <li><strong>子智能体（Subagent）</strong>：Codex 为处理某项具体任务而启动的受委派智能体。</li> <li><strong>智能体线程（Agent thread）</strong>：子智能体开展工作的线程。受支持的客户端允许你打开这些线程，检查其进度或结果。 补充理解：官方原文中的 <strong>main agent</strong> 指专注于需求、决策和最终输出的主智能体；子智能体则处理被委派的具体工作。</li> </ul> <p>可以把流程理解为：你把任务交给主智能体；主智能体按需派出子智能体；它们分别在线程中工作，再把结果交回主线程。</p> <p><a id=\"triggering-subagent-workflows\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">触发子智能体工作流</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在大多数智能等级下，需要直接要求使用子智能体或并行智能体工作。Ultra 支持主动委派，因此 ChatGPT 可以在适合并行的独立工作有助于提升速度或质量时进行委派，无需另行提出要求。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>直接要求使用子智能体或并行智能体工作。适用的项目或技能指令提出要求时，Codex 也可以进行委派。</p> <p>在实践中，手动触发就是使用直接的指令，例如“启动两个智能体”“并行委派这项工作”或“每个要点使用一个智能体”。因为每个子智能体都会独立使用模型和工具，所以与效果相当的单智能体运行相比，子智能体工作流会消耗更多 token。</p> <p>好的子智能体提示词应说明如何拆分工作、Codex 是否应等所有智能体完成后再继续，以及需要返回怎样的摘要或输出。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review this branch with parallel subagents. Spawn one subagent for security risks, one for test gaps, and one for maintainability. Wait for all three, then summarize the findings by category with file references.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请使用并行子智能体审查这个分支。分别创建一个检查安全风险的子智能体、一个检查测试缺口的子智能体，以及一个检查可维护性的子智能体。等待三者全部完成，再按类别汇总发现，并提供文件引用。</div></div> <p><a id=\"choosing-models-and-reasoning\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">选择模型与推理强度</h2> <p>不同的智能体需要不同的模型和推理设置。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在 ChatGPT Work 中，可从输入框选择模型和智能等级。根据所选模型，可用的智能等级可能包括 <strong>Light</strong>、<strong>Medium</strong>、<strong>High</strong>、<strong>Extra High</strong> 和 <strong>Max</strong>。<strong>Ultra</strong> 仅向符合条件的账户和受支持的模型提供。它会使用最高推理强度，并允许 ChatGPT 主动把适合的工作委派给子智能体。</p> <p>在其他智能等级下，如果需要并行委派工作，请明确要求使用子智能体。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>如果没有配置子智能体模型或 <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>，子智能体会继承父智能体的模型和推理强度。如果显式启动请求或 <code>[agents]</code> 默认设置选择了模型，却没有显式指定或配置推理强度，子智能体会使用该模型的默认推理强度。为了根据每项任务平衡智能程度、速度与价格，你可以在提示词中要求特定模型或推理强度，配置 <code>[agents]</code> 默认设置（位于 <code>config.toml</code>），或直接在自定义智能体文件中设置 <code>model</code> 和 <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>。 例如，对于快速扫描，可使用 <code>gpt-6-luna</code>；对于需要更强推理能力的任务，可使用 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> 配置，并选择更高的推理强度。</p> <p>对于 Codex 中的大多数任务，如果你登录的账号或工作区<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">有权限</a>，可以从 <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> 开始。否则请选择你可以使用的模型。对于较轻量的子智能体工作，若希望速度更快、成本更低，可使用 <code>gpt-6-luna</code>。</p> <p><a id=\"model-choice\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_7\">模型选择</h3> <ul> <li><strong><code>gpt-6.1-sol</code></strong>：要求较高的智能体任务可从这里开始。适合需要规划、使用工具、验证，并在较大上下文中持续跟进的模糊、多步骤工作。</li> <li><strong><code>gpt-6-luna</code></strong>：适合快速处理范围窄、要求明确、可重复或工作量大的任务。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"reasoning-effort-model_reasoning_effort\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"model_reasoning_effort\">推理强度（<code>model_reasoning_effort</code>）</h3> <p>对于 GPT-6.1 Sol，请选择你的客户端和所选模型支持的推理强度。显式配置时，可以从 GPT-6 Luna 的 <code>high</code> 或 GPT-6 Astra 的 <code>low</code> 开始，再根据任务调整为所选模型支持的等级。</p> <ul> <li><strong><code>ultra</code></strong>：当所选模型支持时，用于需要最深度推理的任务。</li> <li><strong><code>max</code></strong> 和 <strong><code>xhigh</code></strong>：当所选模型支持时，用于推理要求特别高的任务。</li> <li><strong><code>high</code></strong>：适合需要追踪复杂逻辑、检查假设或处理边界情况的智能体（例如审查或安全类智能体）。</li> <li><strong><code>medium</code></strong>：平衡速度与深度。</li> <li><strong><code>low</code></strong>：适合任务简单直接且速度最重要的情况。</li> </ul> <p>更高的推理强度会增加响应时间和 token 用量，但也可能提高复杂工作的质量。详情请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">模型</a>、<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">配置基础</a>和<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"orchestration-and-thread-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_8\">编排与线程控制</h2> <p>ChatGPT 或 Codex 会处理智能体之间的编排工作，包括启动新的子智能体、转发后续指令、等待结果以及关闭智能体线程。</p> <p>当多个智能体正在运行时，Codex 会等待所有请求的结果就绪，再返回整合后的回复。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在大多数智能等级下，ChatGPT 会在收到直接请求后启动智能体。使用 Ultra 时，如果并行工作有帮助，ChatGPT 也可以主动委派。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>当前 Codex 本地版本会在收到直接请求或适用的项目或技能指令后启动智能体。</p> <p>要查看实际效果，可以在你的项目中尝试以下提示词：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">I would like to review the following points on the current PR (this branch vs main). Spawn one agent per point, wait for all of them, and summarize the result for each point.\n1. Security issue\n2. Code quality\n3. Bugs\n4. Race\n5. Test flakiness\n6. Maintainability of the code\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">我想针对当前 PR（这个分支相对于 main）审查以下各点。为每一点创建一个智能体，等待所有智能体完成，再分别汇总每一点的结果。\n1. 安全问题\n2. 代码质量\n3. 缺陷\n4. 竞态条件\n5. 测试不稳定性\n6. 代码的可维护性</div></div> <p><a id=\"managing-subagents\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_9\">管理子智能体</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>打开 <strong>Subagents</strong>，可查看只读的 <strong>Active</strong> 和 <strong>Done</strong> 列表。选择已完成的子智能体，即可检查其详细信息和结果。网页侧边栏会报告子智能体的活动，但不提供停止或引导单个子智能体的控制功能。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>从主线程中显示的活动打开子智能体线程，检查其工作。</li> <li>直接要求 Codex 引导正在运行的子智能体、停止它，或关闭已完成的子智能体线程。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>插图：Codex 桌面应用聊天中，两个子智能体正在并行工作。</p> <p>插图：Codex 桌面应用的 Subagents 面板中没有正在运行的子智能体，并显示了三个已完成的审计。</p> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>在 CLI 中使用 <code>/subagents</code>，可在正在运行的子智能体线程之间切换，并检查当前线程。</li> <li>直接要求 Codex 引导正在运行的子智能体、停止它，或关闭已完成的智能体线程。</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>当后台智能体面板可用时，展开它即可检查状态、停止正在运行的子智能体，或打开某个子智能体线程。</li> <li>直接要求 Codex 引导正在运行的子智能体、停止它，或关闭已完成的子智能体线程。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"approvals-and-sandbox-controls\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_10\">审批与沙箱控制</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>子智能体会继承你当前的沙箱策略。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work 会在其托管环境中运行子智能体，不提供本地 Codex 沙箱或审批模式控制。子智能体可使用父聊天拥有的工具。网站和连接器权限仍由具体工具决定。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>子智能体会继承输入框下方所选择的权限模式。在要求 Codex 委派工作前，请先为父级轮次选择权限模式。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>在交互式 CLI 会话中，即使你正在查看主线程，非活动智能体线程发出的审批请求也可能出现。审批浮层会显示请求来源的线程标签；在批准、拒绝或回答请求前，可以按 <code>o</code> 打开该线程。</p> <p>在非交互式流程中，或每当某次运行无法呈现新的审批请求时，需要新审批的操作会失败，Codex 会把错误反馈给父级工作流。</p> <p>子智能体会继承父级轮次当前的沙箱和审批设置，包括通过 <code>/permissions</code> 或 <code>--yolo</code> 所做的更改。自定义智能体文件不能替换这些设置。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>子智能体会继承输入框下方所选择的权限模式。在要求 Codex 委派工作前，请先为父级轮次选择权限模式。</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>适用界面：app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>请在父会话中设置沙箱和审批控制。你可以在自定义智能体指令中要求它不要编辑文件，但这不会为它创建独立的只读沙箱。</p> <h2 id=\"_11\">自定义智能体</h2> <p>Codex 随附以下内置智能体：</p> <ul> <li><code>default</code>：通用后备智能体。</li> <li><code>worker</code>：专注于实施和修复的执行型智能体。</li> <li><code>explorer</code>：以读取为主的代码库探索智能体。</li> </ul> <p>要定义自己的自定义智能体，请将独立的 TOML 文件放在 <code>~/.codex/agents/</code>（个人智能体）或 <code>.codex/agents/</code>（项目范围的智能体）下。</p> <p>每个文件定义一个自定义智能体。自定义智能体可以更改模型设置和指令，也可以关闭受支持的能力。它们会继承父级的权限、提供方和 MCP 服务器；自定义智能体文件不能覆盖这些设置。</p> <p>每个独立的自定义智能体文件都必须定义：</p> <ul> <li><code>name</code></li> <li><code>description</code></li> <li><code>developer_instructions</code></li> </ul> <p>如果自定义智能体文件设置了 <code>model</code> 或 <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>，以文件中的值为准。应用该文件之前，Codex 会依次从显式启动值、相应的 <code>[agents]</code> 默认值和父智能体的值中解析各项设置。如果显式启动请求或 <code>[agents]</code> 默认值选择了模型，但两者都没有提供推理强度，Codex 会使用该模型的默认推理强度。只设置了 <code>model</code> 的自定义智能体文件会保留此前解析得到的推理强度。如果所选模型不支持该推理强度，或者你想使用其他等级，也请在文件中设置 <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>。技能会从父级继承；自定义智能体可以通过 <code>skills.config</code> 关闭单项技能。</p> <p><a id=\"global-settings\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_12\">全局设置</h3> <p>子智能体的全局设置仍位于<a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">配置</a>中的 <code>[agents]</code> 下。</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>字段</th> <th>类型</th> <th>必需</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>agents.enabled</code></td> <td>boolean</td> <td>否</td> <td>启用或禁用多智能体工具。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session</code></td> <td>number</td> <td>否</td> <td>限制同时打开的已启动智能体线程数量，不包括主线程。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.default_subagent_model</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>否</td> <td>设置已启动智能体所使用的默认模型。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.default_subagent_reasoning_effort</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>否</td> <td>设置子智能体的默认推理强度。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.interrupt_message</code></td> <td>boolean</td> <td>否</td> <td>智能体轮次被中断时，记录一条模型可见的消息。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><strong>说明：</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>agents.enabled</code> 默认为 <code>true</code>。将其设为 <code>false</code> 可禁用多智能体工具。</li> <li>未设置 <code>agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session</code> 时，Codex 会选择默认值。现有配置可以继续使用 <code>agents.max_threads</code> 这一旧版别名。</li> <li>显式启动值会覆盖 <code>agents.default_subagent_model</code> 和 <code>agents.default_subagent_reasoning_effort</code>。</li> <li><code>agents.interrupt_message</code> 默认为 <code>true</code>。将其设为 <code>false</code> 可使智能体上下文不包含模型可见的中断消息。</li> <li>如果自定义智能体名称与 <code>explorer</code> 等内置智能体相同，将优先使用自定义智能体。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"custom-agent-file-schema\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_13\">自定义智能体文件架构</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>字段</th> <th>类型</th> <th>必需</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>name</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>是</td> <td>Codex 在启动或指代该智能体时使用的名称。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>description</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>是</td> <td>面向用户的说明，用于指示何时应使用该智能体。</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>developer_instructions</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>是</td> <td>定义智能体行为的核心指令。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>使用 <code>model</code>、<code>model_reasoning_effort</code>、<code>model_reasoning_summary</code> 和 <code>model_verbosity</code> 可以自定义模型行为。可接受的取值请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">配置参考</a>。</p> <p>若要减少自定义智能体的能力，可将受支持的功能键设为 <code>false</code>：<code>features.shell_tool</code>、<code>features.apps</code>、<code>features.plugins</code>、<code>features.memories</code> 或 <code>features.request_permissions_tool</code>。使用 <code>skills.config</code> 可关闭单项技能；使用 <code>skills.bundled.enabled = false</code> 可关闭内置技能。设置 <code>skills.include_instructions = false</code> 可省略自动添加的技能指令块。托管要求仍然适用。</p> <p>其他会话设置（包括 <code>sandbox_mode</code>、<code>approval_policy</code>、<code>model_provider</code> 和 <code>mcp_servers</code>）即使写在自定义智能体文件中，也不会覆盖父级配置。服务层级也遵循根会话的偏好。请在父会话中配置 MCP 服务器，以便子智能体使用。</p> <p>Codex 通过 <code>name</code> 字段识别自定义智能体。让文件名与智能体名称一致是最简单的约定，但以 <code>name</code> 字段为准。</p> <p><a id=\"example-custom-agents\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_14\">自定义智能体示例</h3> <p>最好的自定义智能体通常职责明确、观点鲜明。请为每个智能体安排清晰的工作、提供与其职责匹配的工具范围，并通过指令防止它偏离到相邻工作。</p> <p><a id=\"example-1-pr-review\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"1pr\">示例 1：PR 审查</h4> <p>如果你登录的账号或工作区有权限，以下示例会使用 <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a>。如果无法使用，请选择你有权限使用的模型。</p> <p>以下模式将审查工作拆分给三个各有侧重的自定义智能体：</p> <ul> <li><code>pr_explorer</code> 负责梳理代码库并收集证据。</li> <li><code>reviewer</code> 负责查找正确性、安全性与测试方面的风险。</li> <li><code>docs_researcher</code> 通过专用 MCP 服务器核对框架或 API 文档。</li> </ul> <p>项目配置（<code>.codex/config.toml</code>）：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[agents]\nmax_concurrent_threads_per_session = 8\n\n[mcp_servers.openaiDeveloperDocs]\nurl = \"https://developers.openai.com/mcp\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/pr-explorer.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"pr_explorer\"\ndescription = \"Read-only codebase explorer for gathering evidence before changes are proposed.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nStay in exploration mode.\nDo not edit files.\nTrace the real execution path, cite files and symbols, and avoid proposing fixes unless the parent agent asks for them.\nPrefer fast search and targeted file reads over broad scans.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/reviewer.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"reviewer\"\ndescription = \"PR reviewer focused on correctness, security, and missing tests.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6.1-sol\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nReview code like an owner.\nDo not edit files.\nPrioritize correctness, security, behavior regressions, and missing test coverage.\nLead with concrete findings, include reproduction steps when possible, and avoid style-only comments unless they hide a real bug.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/docs-researcher.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"docs_researcher\"\ndescription = \"Documentation specialist that uses the docs MCP server to verify APIs and framework behavior.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nUse the docs MCP server to confirm APIs, options, and version-specific behavior.\nReturn concise answers with links or exact references when available.\nDo not make code changes.\n\"\"\"\n\n</code></pre> <p>这种设置很适合下面这样的提示词：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review this branch against main. Have pr_explorer map the affected code paths, reviewer find real risks, and docs_researcher verify the framework APIs that the patch relies on.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请对照 main 审查这个分支。让 pr_explorer 梳理受影响的代码路径，让 reviewer 查找实际风险，让 docs_researcher 核实补丁所依赖的框架 API。</div></div> <p><a id=\"example-2-frontend-integration-debugging\"></a></p> <h4 id=\"2\">示例 2：前端集成调试</h4> <p>以下模式适合排查 UI 回归、偶发的浏览器流程问题，或横跨应用代码与运行中产品的集成错误。</p> <p>项目配置（<code>.codex/config.toml</code>）：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[agents]\nmax_concurrent_threads_per_session = 6\n\n[mcp_servers.chrome_devtools]\nurl = \"http://localhost:3000/mcp\"\nstartup_timeout_sec = 20\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/code-mapper.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"code_mapper\"\ndescription = \"Read-only codebase explorer for locating the relevant frontend and backend code paths.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nMap the code that owns the failing UI flow.\nDo not edit files.\nIdentify entry points, state transitions, and likely files before the worker starts editing.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/browser-debugger.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"browser_debugger\"\ndescription = \"UI debugger that uses browser tooling to reproduce issues and capture evidence.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6.1-sol\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nReproduce the issue in the browser, capture exact steps, and report what the UI actually does.\nUse browser tooling for screenshots, console output, and network evidence.\nDo not edit application code.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/ui-fixer.toml</code>：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"ui_fixer\"\ndescription = \"Implementation-focused agent for small, targeted fixes after the issue is understood.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nOwn the fix once the issue is reproduced.\nMake the smallest defensible change, keep unrelated files untouched, and validate only the behavior you changed.\n\"\"\"\n\n[[skills.config]]\npath = \"/Users/me/.agents/skills/docs-editor/SKILL.md\"\nenabled = false\n</code></pre> <p>这种设置很适合下面这样的提示词：</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Investigate why the settings modal fails to save. Have browser_debugger reproduce it, code_mapper trace the responsible code path, and ui_fixer implement the smallest fix once the failure mode is clear.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">请调查设置弹窗为何无法保存。让 browser_debugger 复现问题，让 code_mapper 追踪相关代码路径，并在明确故障机制后，让 ui_fixer 实施最小修复。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"subagents\">Subagents</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work and Codex can run subagent workflows by spawning specialized agents in parallel and then collecting their results in one response. This can be particularly helpful for complex tasks that are highly parallel, such as codebase exploration or implementing a multi-step feature plan.</p> <p>In local Codex clients, you can also define custom agents with different model configurations and instructions for different tasks.</p> <h2 id=\"availability\">Availability</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work exposes subagent workflows and activity to eligible accounts.</p> <p><a id=\"custom-agents\"></a></p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Current Codex releases enable subagent workflows by default. Subagent activity appears in the ChatGPT desktop app, Codex CLI, and the IDE extension.</p> <p>Because each subagent does its own model and tool work, subagent workflows consume more tokens than comparable single-agent runs.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In ChatGPT Work, ask ChatGPT to delegate independent work to subagents. The agents run in ChatGPT's hosted environment, and the chat shows their activity and results. At most intelligence levels, ask for delegation explicitly. With Ultra, ChatGPT can proactively delegate work when parallel agents would materially improve speed or quality.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Ask Codex in an app chat to delegate independent parts of the work to subagents. Current local Codex releases delegate when you ask directly or when applicable <code>AGENTS.md</code> or skill instructions request it. The app surfaces each subagent thread so you can inspect its work and the summary returned to the main chat.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Ask Codex in an interactive CLI session to use subagents. Codex can also follow applicable <code>AGENTS.md</code> or skill instructions that request delegation. Use <code>/subagents</code> to inspect and switch between agent threads while they run. The main thread collects the subagent results into its final response.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Ask Codex in an IDE chat to delegate independent parts of the work to subagents. Codex can also follow applicable <code>AGENTS.md</code> or skill instructions that request delegation. When the background-agent UI is available, active subagents appear above the composer. Expand the panel to see their status, stop all active subagents, or open an individual subagent thread.</p> <h2 id=\"why-subagent-workflows-help\">Why subagent workflows help</h2> <p>Even with large context windows, models have limits. If you flood the main chat (where you're defining requirements, constraints, and decisions) with noisy intermediate output such as exploration notes, test logs, stack traces, and command output, the session can become less reliable over time.</p> <p>This is often described as:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Context pollution</strong>: useful information gets buried under noisy intermediate output.</li> <li><strong>Context rot</strong>: performance degrades as the chat fills up with less relevant details.</li> </ul> <p>For background, see the Chroma writeup on <a href=\"https://research.trychroma.com/context-rot\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">context rot (online)</a>.</p> <p>Subagent workflows help by moving noisy work off the main thread:</p> <ul> <li>Keep the <strong>main agent</strong> focused on requirements, decisions, and final outputs.</li> <li>Run specialized <strong>subagents</strong> in parallel for exploration, tests, or log analysis.</li> <li>Return <strong>summaries</strong> from subagents instead of raw intermediate output.</li> </ul> <p>They can also save time when the work can run independently in parallel, and they make larger-shaped tasks more tractable by breaking them into bounded pieces. For example, Codex can split analysis of a multi-million-token document into smaller problems and return distilled takeaways to the main thread.</p> <p>As a starting point, use parallel agents for read-heavy tasks such as exploration, tests, triage, and summarization. Be more careful with parallel write-heavy workflows, because agents editing code at once can create conflicts and increase coordination overhead.</p> <h2 id=\"core-terms\">Core terms</h2> <p>Codex uses a few related terms in subagent workflows:</p> <ul> <li><strong>Subagent workflow</strong>: A workflow where Codex runs parallel agents and combines their results.</li> <li><strong>Subagent</strong>: A delegated agent that Codex starts to handle a specific task.</li> <li><strong>Agent thread</strong>: The thread where a subagent does its work. Supported clients let you open these threads to inspect progress or results.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"triggering-subagent-workflows\">Triggering subagent workflows</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>At most intelligence levels, ask for subagents or parallel agent work directly. Ultra enables proactive delegation, so ChatGPT can delegate suitable independent work without a separate request.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Ask for subagents or parallel agent work directly. Codex can also delegate when applicable project or skill instructions request it.</p> <p>In practice, manual triggering means using direct instructions such as \"spawn two agents,\" \"delegate this work in parallel,\" or \"use one agent per point.\" Subagent workflows consume more tokens than comparable single-agent runs because each subagent does its own model and tool work.</p> <p>A good subagent prompt should explain how to divide the work, whether Codex should wait for all agents before continuing, and what summary or output to return.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review this branch with parallel subagents. Spawn one subagent for security risks, one for test gaps, and one for maintainability. Wait for all three, then summarize the findings by category with file references.\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"choosing-models-and-reasoning\">Choosing models and reasoning</h2> <p>Different agents need different model and reasoning settings.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In ChatGPT Work, choose a model and an intelligence level from the composer. Available intelligence levels can include <strong>Light</strong>, <strong>Medium</strong>, <strong>High</strong>, <strong>Extra High</strong>, and <strong>Max</strong>, depending on the selected model. <strong>Ultra</strong> is available only to eligible accounts and supported models. It uses maximum reasoning and lets ChatGPT proactively delegate suitable work to subagents.</p> <p>At other intelligence levels, ask for subagents explicitly when you want work delegated in parallel.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>If you don't configure a subagent model or <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>, the subagent inherits the parent agent's model and reasoning effort. If an explicit spawn request or an <code>[agents]</code> default selects a model without an explicit or configured reasoning effort, the subagent uses that model's default reasoning effort. To balance intelligence, speed, and price for each task, request a specific model or reasoning effort in your prompt, configure <code>[agents]</code> defaults in <code>config.toml</code>, or set <code>model</code> and <code>model_reasoning_effort</code> directly in the custom agent file. For example, use <code>gpt-6-luna</code> for fast scans or a higher-effort <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> configuration for more demanding reasoning.</p> <p>For most tasks in Codex, start with <code>gpt-6.1-sol</code> when your signed-in account or workspace has <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">access</a>. Otherwise, choose a model available to you. Use <code>gpt-6-luna</code> when you want a faster, lower-cost option for lighter subagent work.</p> <h3 id=\"model-choice\">Model choice</h3> <ul> <li><strong><code>gpt-6.1-sol</code></strong>: Start here for demanding agents. Use it for ambiguous, multi-step work that needs planning, tool use, validation, and follow-through across a larger context.</li> <li><strong><code>gpt-6-luna</code></strong>: Use for fast, narrowly scoped agents handling clear, repeatable, or high-volume work.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"reasoning-effort-model_reasoning_effort\">Reasoning effort (<code>model_reasoning_effort</code>)</h3> <p>For GPT-6.1 Sol, use a reasoning effort supported by your client and selected model. For explicit model settings, start with <code>high</code> for GPT-6 Luna or <code>low</code> for GPT-6 Astra. Adjust for the task using a level the selected model supports.</p> <ul> <li><strong><code>ultra</code></strong>: Use for the deepest reasoning when the selected model supports it.</li> <li><strong><code>max</code></strong> and <strong><code>xhigh</code></strong>: Use for especially demanding reasoning when the selected model supports these levels.</li> <li><strong><code>high</code></strong>: Use when an agent needs to trace complex logic, check assumptions, or work through edge cases (for example, reviewer or security-focused agents).</li> <li><strong><code>medium</code></strong>: Balances speed and depth.</li> <li><strong><code>low</code></strong>: Use when the task is straightforward and speed matters most.</li> </ul> <p>Higher reasoning effort increases response time and token usage, but it can improve quality for complex work. For details, see <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938\">Models</a>, <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76\">Config basics</a>, and <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">Configuration Reference</a>.</p> <h2 id=\"orchestration-and-thread-controls\">Orchestration and thread controls</h2> <p>ChatGPT or Codex handles orchestration across agents, including spawning new subagents, routing follow-up instructions, waiting for results, and closing agent threads.</p> <p>When many agents are running, Codex waits until all requested results are available, then returns a consolidated response.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>At most intelligence levels, ChatGPT spawns agents after a direct request. With Ultra, ChatGPT can also delegate proactively when parallel work is useful.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Current local Codex releases spawn agents after a direct request or applicable project or skill instruction.</p> <p>To see it in action, try the following prompt on your project:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">I would like to review the following points on the current PR (this branch vs main). Spawn one agent per point, wait for all of them, and summarize the result for each point.\n1. Security issue\n2. Code quality\n3. Bugs\n4. Race\n5. Test flakiness\n6. Maintainability of the code\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"managing-subagents\">Managing subagents</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Open <strong>Subagents</strong> to see read-only <strong>Active</strong> and <strong>Done</strong> lists. Select a completed subagent to inspect its details and result. The web sidebar reports subagent activity; it doesn't provide controls to stop or steer an individual subagent.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>Open a subagent thread from the activity shown in the main thread to inspect its work.</li> <li>Ask Codex directly to steer a running subagent, stop it, or close completed subagent threads.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>Illustration: Codex desktop chat showing two subagents working in parallel.</p> <p>Illustration: Codex desktop Subagents panel with no active subagents and three completed audits.</p> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>Use <code>/subagents</code> in the CLI to switch between active agent threads and inspect the ongoing thread.</li> <li>Ask Codex directly to steer a running subagent, stop it, or close completed agent threads.</li> </ul> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <ul> <li>When the background-agent panel is available, expand it to inspect status, stop active subagents, or open a subagent thread.</li> <li>Ask Codex directly to steer a running subagent, stop it, or close completed subagent threads.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"approvals-and-sandbox-controls\">Approvals and sandbox controls</h2> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Subagents inherit your current sandbox policy.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: web</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>ChatGPT Work runs subagents in its hosted environment and doesn't expose a local Codex sandbox or approval-mode control. Subagents use the tools available to the parent chat. Website and connector permissions remain tool-specific.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Subagents inherit the permission mode selected beneath the composer. Choose the permission mode for the parent turn before you ask Codex to delegate work.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: cli</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>In interactive CLI sessions, approval requests can surface from inactive agent threads even while you are looking at the main thread. The approval overlay shows the source thread label, and you can press <code>o</code> to open that thread before you approve, reject, or answer the request.</p> <p>In non-interactive flows, or whenever a run can't surface a fresh approval, an action that needs new approval fails and Codex surfaces the error back to the parent workflow.</p> <p>Subagents inherit the parent turn's current sandbox and approval settings, including changes made with <code>/permissions</code> or <code>--yolo</code>. A custom agent file can't replace those settings.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Subagents inherit the permission mode selected beneath the composer. Choose the permission mode for the parent turn before you ask Codex to delegate work.</p> <blockquote> <p><strong>Surface: app,cli,ide</strong></p> </blockquote> <p>Set sandbox and approval controls on the parent session. Custom agent instructions can ask an agent to avoid edits, but they don't create a separate read-only sandbox.</p> <h2 id=\"custom-agents\">Custom agents</h2> <p>Codex ships with built-in agents:</p> <ul> <li><code>default</code>: general-purpose fallback agent.</li> <li><code>worker</code>: execution-focused agent for implementation and fixes.</li> <li><code>explorer</code>: read-heavy codebase exploration agent.</li> </ul> <p>To define your own custom agents, add standalone TOML files under <code>~/.codex/agents/</code> for personal agents or <code>.codex/agents/</code> for project-scoped agents.</p> <p>Each file defines one custom agent. Custom agents can change model settings and instructions or disable supported capabilities. They inherit the parent's permissions, provider, and MCP servers; a custom agent file can't override those settings.</p> <p>Every standalone custom agent file must define:</p> <ul> <li><code>name</code></li> <li><code>description</code></li> <li><code>developer_instructions</code></li> </ul> <p>If a custom agent file sets <code>model</code> or <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>, the value in the file takes precedence. Before applying the file, Codex resolves each setting from an explicit spawn value, then the corresponding <code>[agents]</code> default, then the parent's value. If an explicit spawn request or an <code>[agents]</code> default selects a model and neither supplies a reasoning effort, Codex uses that model's default effort. A custom agent file that sets only <code>model</code> preserves this previously resolved effort. Set <code>model_reasoning_effort</code> in the file too if the selected model doesn't support that effort or you want a different one. Skills inherit from the parent, and a custom agent can disable individual skills with <code>skills.config</code>.</p> <h3 id=\"global-settings\">Global settings</h3> <p>Global subagent settings still live under <code>[agents]</code> in your <a href=\"#/article/a-d684e38d0094ab76?anchor=configuration-precedence\">configuration</a>.</p> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Type</th> <th>Required</th> <th>Purpose</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>agents.enabled</code></td> <td>boolean</td> <td>No</td> <td>Enable or disable multi-agent tools.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session</code></td> <td>number</td> <td>No</td> <td>Cap concurrently open spawned-agent threads, excluding the primary.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.default_subagent_model</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>No</td> <td>Set the default model for spawned agents.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.default_subagent_reasoning_effort</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>No</td> <td>Set the default reasoning effort for spawned agents.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>agents.interrupt_message</code></td> <td>boolean</td> <td>No</td> <td>Record a model-visible message when an agent turn is interrupted.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><strong>Notes:</strong></p> <ul> <li><code>agents.enabled</code> defaults to <code>true</code>. Set it to <code>false</code> to disable multi-agent tools.</li> <li>When you leave <code>agents.max_concurrent_threads_per_session</code> unset, Codex chooses the default. Existing configurations can keep using <code>agents.max_threads</code> as a legacy alias.</li> <li>Explicit spawn values override <code>agents.default_subagent_model</code> and <code>agents.default_subagent_reasoning_effort</code>.</li> <li><code>agents.interrupt_message</code> defaults to <code>true</code>. Set it to <code>false</code> to omit the model-visible interruption message from the agent's context.</li> <li>If a custom agent name matches a built-in agent such as <code>explorer</code>, your custom agent takes precedence.</li> </ul> <h3 id=\"custom-agent-file-schema\">Custom agent file schema</h3> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Field</th> <th>Type</th> <th>Required</th> <th>Purpose</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><code>name</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>Yes</td> <td>Agent name Codex uses when spawning or referring to this agent.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>description</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>Yes</td> <td>Human-facing guidance for when Codex should use this agent.</td> </tr> <tr> <td><code>developer_instructions</code></td> <td>string</td> <td>Yes</td> <td>Core instructions that define the agent's behavior.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p>Use <code>model</code>, <code>model_reasoning_effort</code>, <code>model_reasoning_summary</code>, and <code>model_verbosity</code> to customize model behavior. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-c2332644faa13713\">configuration reference</a> for their accepted values.</p> <p>To reduce a custom agent's capabilities, set supported feature keys to <code>false</code>: <code>features.shell_tool</code>, <code>features.apps</code>, <code>features.plugins</code>, <code>features.memories</code>, or <code>features.request_permissions_tool</code>. Disable individual skills with <code>skills.config</code> or bundled skills with <code>skills.bundled.enabled = false</code>. Set <code>skills.include_instructions = false</code> to omit the automatic skills instructions block. Managed requirements still apply.</p> <p>Other session settings, including <code>sandbox_mode</code>, <code>approval_policy</code>, <code>model_provider</code>, and <code>mcp_servers</code>, don't override the parent configuration when placed in a custom agent file. The service tier also follows the root session's preference. Configure MCP servers in the parent session so the agent can use them.</p> <p>Codex identifies the custom agent by its <code>name</code> field. Matching the filename to the agent name is the simplest convention, but the <code>name</code> field is the source of truth.</p> <h3 id=\"example-custom-agents\">Example custom agents</h3> <p>The best custom agents are narrow and opinionated. Give each one clear job, a tool surface that matches that job, and instructions that keep it from drifting into adjacent work.</p> <p>The examples use <a href=\"#/article/a-ae24d057324a4938?anchor=gpt-6.1-sol\">GPT-6.1 Sol</a> where your signed-in account or workspace has access. If it isn't available, choose a model you can use.</p> <h4 id=\"example-1-pr-review\">Example 1: PR review</h4> <p>This pattern splits review across three focused custom agents:</p> <ul> <li><code>pr_explorer</code> maps the codebase and gathers evidence.</li> <li><code>reviewer</code> looks for correctness, security, and test risks.</li> <li><code>docs_researcher</code> checks framework or API documentation through a dedicated MCP server.</li> </ul> <p>Project config (<code>.codex/config.toml</code>):</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[agents]\nmax_concurrent_threads_per_session = 8\n\n[mcp_servers.openaiDeveloperDocs]\nurl = \"https://developers.openai.com/mcp\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/pr-explorer.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"pr_explorer\"\ndescription = \"Read-only codebase explorer for gathering evidence before changes are proposed.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nStay in exploration mode.\nDo not edit files.\nTrace the real execution path, cite files and symbols, and avoid proposing fixes unless the parent agent asks for them.\nPrefer fast search and targeted file reads over broad scans.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/reviewer.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"reviewer\"\ndescription = \"PR reviewer focused on correctness, security, and missing tests.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6.1-sol\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nReview code like an owner.\nDo not edit files.\nPrioritize correctness, security, behavior regressions, and missing test coverage.\nLead with concrete findings, include reproduction steps when possible, and avoid style-only comments unless they hide a real bug.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/docs-researcher.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"docs_researcher\"\ndescription = \"Documentation specialist that uses the docs MCP server to verify APIs and framework behavior.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nUse the docs MCP server to confirm APIs, options, and version-specific behavior.\nReturn concise answers with links or exact references when available.\nDo not make code changes.\n\"\"\"\n\n</code></pre> <p>This setup works well for prompts like:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Review this branch against main. Have pr_explorer map the affected code paths, reviewer find real risks, and docs_researcher verify the framework APIs that the patch relies on.\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"example-2-frontend-integration-debugging\">Example 2: Frontend integration debugging</h4> <p>This pattern is useful for UI regressions, flaky browser flows, or integration bugs that cross application code and the running product.</p> <p>Project config (<code>.codex/config.toml</code>):</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">[agents]\nmax_concurrent_threads_per_session = 6\n\n[mcp_servers.chrome_devtools]\nurl = \"http://localhost:3000/mcp\"\nstartup_timeout_sec = 20\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/code-mapper.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"code_mapper\"\ndescription = \"Read-only codebase explorer for locating the relevant frontend and backend code paths.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nMap the code that owns the failing UI flow.\nDo not edit files.\nIdentify entry points, state transitions, and likely files before the worker starts editing.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/browser-debugger.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"browser_debugger\"\ndescription = \"UI debugger that uses browser tooling to reproduce issues and capture evidence.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6.1-sol\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"medium\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nReproduce the issue in the browser, capture exact steps, and report what the UI actually does.\nUse browser tooling for screenshots, console output, and network evidence.\nDo not edit application code.\n\"\"\"\n</code></pre> <p><code>.codex/agents/ui-fixer.toml</code>:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-toml\">name = \"ui_fixer\"\ndescription = \"Implementation-focused agent for small, targeted fixes after the issue is understood.\"\nmodel = \"gpt-6-luna\"\nmodel_reasoning_effort = \"high\"\ndeveloper_instructions = \"\"\"\nOwn the fix once the issue is reproduced.\nMake the smallest defensible change, keep unrelated files untouched, and validate only the behavior you changed.\n\"\"\"\n\n[[skills.config]]\npath = \"/Users/me/.agents/skills/docs-editor/SKILL.md\"\nenabled = false\n</code></pre> <p>This setup works well for prompts like:</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Investigate why the settings modal fails to save. Have browser_debugger reproduce it, code_mapper trace the responsible code path, and ui_fixer implement the smallest fix once the failure mode is clear.\n</code></pre>"};
